carmen: Need a tiny migration note for v1->v2: very short para, one TS + one Py fallback snippet (only on 5xx/network), one-line curl smoke test, and a support ticket template. Who can own?

phil: I can. Will keep it minimal and safety-first.

phil: Draft para: When moving from redwood-v1 to redwood-v2, canary traffic and validate outputs. Use an availability fallback that only triggers on network/5xx errors to avoid masking auth/client problems. If using embeddings, verify vector dimensions before switching; re-encode or pin the model to avoid retrieval regressions.

phil: TS snippet:
```ts
import { Client } from '@redwood/inference'
const c = new Client()
async function gen(p){
  try { return await c.generate({model:'redwood-v2', input:p}) }
  catch(e:any){ if (e.status && e.status >= 500) return c.generate({model:'redwood-v1', input:p}); throw e }
}
```

phil: Py snippet:
```py
from redwood import Client
c = Client()
def gen(p):
    try:
        return c.generate(model='redwood-v2', input=p)
    except Exception as e:
        if getattr(e, 'status', 0) >= 500:
            return c.generate(model='redwood-v1', input=p)
        raise
```

phil: Curl smoke test (one line):
`curl -sS -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/generate -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -d '{"model":"redwood-v2","input":"ping"}' || curl -sS -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/generate -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -d '{"model":"redwood-v1","input":"ping"}'`

